Third-party algorithm references
================================

The `src/sparse_attention/` module is a Rust-from-scratch port of the
algorithm and tensor contracts described in the following upstream projects.
None of their source code is vendored or copied — only the mathematical
formulation, the CSR inverse-index construction, the KV-outer scheduling
strategy, and the LSE-combine identity are used. Any similarity in
identifier naming (e.g. `kvouter_attention`, `build_kvouter_index`,
`sparse_topk_select`) is intentional so that readers cross-checking against
the upstream documentation can navigate this crate.

  * MiniMax Sparse Attention (MSA)
    Repository: https://github.com/MiniMax-AI/MSA
    License:    MIT
    Copyright:  MiniMax
    Reference:  docs/MiniMaxSparseAttention.pdf (upstream repository)

  * MiniMax kernels for M3 KV-outer sparse attention
    Repository: https://github.com/fw-ai/minimax-kernels
    License:    Apache License 2.0
    Copyright:  Fireworks AI, Inc.
    Reference:  docs/m3-sparse-attention.md (upstream repository)

  * FlashAttention-4 (algorithm foundation for the persistent SM100 forward
    referenced by fw-ai/minimax-kernels).
    Repository: https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention
    License:    BSD 3-Clause
